              "title": "LogViewerState protocol width at upper boundary (8 requirements)",
              "issue": "LogViewerState declares 8 requirements (7 properties + 1 method), placing it at the top of the MINOR band (6-8). With only one conformer (LogViewerViewModel) — which achieves 100% coverage — ISP-2 and ISP-3 cannot be fully verified per Exception 3. The protocol mixes at least two distinct conceptual groups: observable view data (messages, displayedMessages, isLoading, taskList, toolResultLookup, pendingPrompt) and navigation/formatting concerns (fileURL, roleLabel). If a second conformer ever needs only the data properties, it would be forced to also implement fileURL and roleLabel, producing low coverage. The width of 8 is also one step away from triggering the SEVERE threshold.",
